.TH USB-SPEED-TESTER 1 "2026-09-25" "usb-speed-tester 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-speed-tester \- analyse, benchmark and diagnose USB storage devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-speed-tester
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-speed-tester
is a PyQt6 desktop application that runs the usual Linux USB diagnostic tools
and explains their output in plain language.
.PP
A device is chosen from a drop\-down list, the tests to run are ticked in a
collapsible panel, and the results appear in two tabs: a
.I "Technical Log"
with the raw command output, and a
.I "User Analysis"
with a short interpretation of what the numbers mean. A third tab,
.IR Explanations ,
contains an illustrated tutorial on how to recognise a USB 3.x SuperSpeed port
by the
.B SS
marking next to the connector.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.SH TESTS
.TP
.B Bus Analysis
Runs
.BR lsusb \-t
and reports whether the device negotiated USB 3.x (5000M) or USB 2.0 (480M).
No privileges are needed.
.TP
.B Read Benchmark
Runs
.BR hdparm \-tT
through
.BR pkexec (1)
to compare cached and physical read speed.
.TP
.B Write Benchmark
Writes a 1 GB test file with
.BR dd (1)
after checking that the device has at least 1.5 GB free.
.TP
.B Fio Benchmark
Runs four
.BR fio (1)
jobs (sequential read and write, 4K random read and write) and reports
throughput, IOPS and latency.
.TP
.B SMART Health
Runs
.B smartctl \-a
through
.BR pkexec (1).
Most USB flash drives use a bridge chip that does not forward SMART data, in
which case the program says so instead of failing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B USB_SPEED_TESTER_DATA
Directory holding the bundled
.IR assets/ ,
.I tutorial/
and
.I translations/
data, overriding the built\-in search path. It is used by the autopkgtest
suite and when running from an unusual layout.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/usb-speed-tester/
Bundled diagrams, tutorial and compiled translations.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/usb-speed-tester/
Copyright and other documentation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program exited normally.
.TP
.B 1
The program was started with an invalid option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsusb (8),
.BR hdparm (8),
.BR dd (1),
.BR fio (1),
.BR smartctl (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
